course: dictionary
lesson: 2169
title: Correct as right and as fix
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word correct has two jobs. As an adjective, it describes something: «the correct answer» is the answer that is right, with no mistakes. As a verb, it is an action: to correct means to find and fix mistakes.
explain: Context tells you which job the word is doing. «Correcting someone in front of everyone often hurts more than the mistake itself.» Correcting is something a person does, so it is the verb. Ask yourself: is the word doing something, or describing a thing?
explain: The verb changes its ending too: correct, corrects, corrected and correcting all come from the same root. «The teacher corrected my spelling» uses the past form. Once you know one form, you can work out the others.
fact: «Correct» means right, true, or without mistakes.
fact: «Correct» can also mean proper or suitable, like «the correct way to behave».
fact: «To correct» means to find and fix mistakes.
fact: A teacher corrects work by marking what is right and wrong.
fact: If the word is doing an action, it is a verb; if it describes a thing, it is an adjective.
exercise: «Both spellings are correct in their own country.» What does correct mean here? | *Right and acceptable | Shorter than the other one | Wrong and must be fixed | Written in red ink
exercise: «Correcting a teacher privately instead of in front of everyone is kind.» Is correcting a verb or an adjective here? | Adjective, because it describes a teacher | *Verb, because it is an action | Adverb, because it tells how | Noun, because it names a thing
exercise: «Correct me if I'm wrong.» What does correct mean in this sentence? | Make me a correct answer | Write my name neatly | *Find and fix my mistakes | Agree with me happily
test: Which word is the verb in «the teacher corrects the homework»? | the | teacher | homework | *corrects
test: In «He wrote the correct answer on the board», what does correct mean? | *Right, without mistakes | Written quickly | To fix a mistake | Loud and clear
exam: Which sentence uses correct as a verb? | Both spellings are correct in their own country. | The correct answer is seven. | That is the correct way to behave. | *Please correct the mistakes on your page.
